Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 14:17:51 +0800
Subject: files: a file that is gone shows in its tab instead of failing

Reading a file from a directory that no longer exists (a reboot cleared
/tmp) answered 500 "Directory not found"; answer 404 FileNotFoundError
like a missing file in an existing directory. And a missing file no
longer toasts "Failed to load file": its tab already shows it (struck-
through name, "File not found"), and a tab restored with the session
toasted on every visit. The tab stays, and loads again once the file is
back. Other read errors still toast.

Ocelot-Patch: web/missing-file

diff --git a/packages/app/src/workspaces/files/model.tsx b/packages/app/src/workspaces/files/model.tsx
index 80fe999ad54b03ba54999840b3d963b4170013a4..aac7a62a4ad0299de6bfcfcade5911ac51e778e2 100644
--- a/packages/app/src/workspaces/files/model.tsx
+++ b/packages/app/src/workspaces/files/model.tsx
@@ -146,6 +146,9 @@ export const { use: useFile, provider: FileProvider } = createSimpleContext({
           draft.content = undefined
         }),
       )
+      // ocelot: a missing file shows in its tab (struck-through name, "not found"); a restored tab
+      // whose file is gone would otherwise toast on every visit.
+      if (notFound) return
       showToast({
         variant: "error",
         title: language.t("toast.file.loadFailed.title"),
